<h1>Tabletop Chain &amp; Mat Top Conveyors</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">A tabletop chain conveyor uses interlocking flat-top links, plastic or stainless steel, to form a smooth, rigid conveying surface that navigates straight runs and horizontal curves without transfers. Side-flexing tabletop chains make tight turns, eliminating the transfer points that cause jams and product damage in bottle, can, and carton handling. Tabletop chain and mat top conveyors dominate <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/beverage/">beverage</a>, dairy, pharmaceutical, and personal care <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/">packaging lines</a> where products must travel complex layouts through fillers, cappers, labelers, and case packers.</p>
<h2 id="types-heading">Tabletop Chain Configurations</h2>
<h3>Straight-Running Chain</h3>
<p>Straight-running tabletop chain travels in straight lines only. The links interlock rigidly and do not articulate laterally. Straight-running chains cost less than side-flexing chains and suit layouts with only straight conveyor sections. Direction changes require right-angle <a href="/conveyor-types/transfer-conveyors/">transfer conveyors</a> or dead plates between separate straight sections. Straight-running chain widths range from 3.25" to over 24" in single-strand and multi-strand configurations.</p>
<h3>Side-Flexing Chain</h3>
<p>Side-flexing tabletop chain articulates laterally, allowing the chain to navigate horizontal curves. The link design includes a pivot feature that permits each link to angle relative to adjacent links. Minimum curve radius depends on chain width, typically 1.5x to 2.5x the chain width. A 4.5"-wide side-flexing chain turns a 9" inside radius. This eliminates transfers at corners, reducing jams, product damage, and floor space. Rexnord (Rex), Regal Rexnord, and <a href="https://www.intralox.com/products/conveyor-belts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Intralox</a> manufacture side-flexing tabletop chains.</p>
<h3>Multi-Flex Chain</h3>
<p>Multi-flex chain flexes both horizontally (side-flex) and vertically, allowing the chain to navigate curves, inclines, and declines in a single continuous run. This eliminates separate incline and curve sections. Multi-flex chains suit compact multi-level layouts where products must travel up, around, and down through processing equipment. Rexnord's MatTop and Intralox's Series configurations include multi-flex options.</p>
<h3>Mat Top (Modular Belt)</h3>
<p>Mat top conveyors use wider <a href="/resources/conveyor-belting/">modular plastic belts</a> made of interlocking injection-molded modules connected by hinge rods. Mat top belts range from 6" to over 60" wide, providing a flat surface for cases, trays, totes, and larger products. Mat top belts offer positive sprocket drive (no slip), easy module replacement (swap individual damaged modules), and surface options including flat, raised-rib, non-slip, and perforated. Intralox, Habasit, and Rexnord are leading mat top belt manufacturers.</p>
